### Revised Rule

The transformation involves two objects: a vertical line of color 8 (blue) and a horizontal line of color 2 (red).  
- Identify the column containing the blue vertical line (all contiguous blue cells in that column).  
- Identify the row containing the red horizontal line (all contiguous red cells in that row).  
- Extend the blue line vertically to fill the entire column, but skip the row occupied by the extended red line (i.e., do not place blue in that row).  
- Extend the red line horizontally to fill the entire row, but skip the column occupied by the extended blue line (i.e., do not place red in that column).  
- At the intersection of the extended blue column and extended red row, set the cell to color 4 (purple).  
- All other cells remain background (0).  

This ensures that the extended colors do not overwrite each other's exclusive row/column except at the intersection, which becomes a distinct color.

