### Proposed Rule  
Given an n×n input grid A, create a 2n×2n output grid as follows:  
1. Let B be the matrix whose rows are the vertically reversed columns of A in original column order (i.e., row i of B = column i of A reversed top-to-bottom).  
2. Place A in the top-left n×n block.  
3. Place B in the top-right n×n block.  
4. Place rotate180(B) in the bottom-left n×n block.  
5. Place rotate180(A) in the bottom-right n×n block.  
(rotate180 means reverse the order of rows and then reverse each row left-to-right.)

