   - If multiple objects map to the same output cell, the one with the larger original row index (or column index, but in practice the later one in reading order) overwrites.

3. **Background**: All cells not occupied by the diagonal or reflected objects become 0.

This rule treats objects as coherent units, reflecting them across the diagonal while preserving contiguity and shape (though the shape may be transposed). It aligns with ARC priors of object persistence and structured geometric transformations.

